# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in real values from your Supabase project settings
# (Project Settings → API). Never commit .env or .env.local — .gitignore already excludes them.
#
# Only the PUBLIC anon key belongs here. The service-role key must never be set as a Vite env
# var (anything prefixed VITE_ is bundled into the browser JS and is publicly readable) — it has
# no legitimate use in this frontend-only app. See SUPABASE_SETUP.md.

VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# Optional. Photos and scanned PDFs are read with Tesseract.js, which downloads its worker, WASM
# core and English data from a public CDN (cdn.jsdelivr.net) the first time. If that CDN is blocked
# where the app is used, host the files yourself and point this at the folder (it must contain
# worker.min.js, core/ with tesseract.js-core's files, and lang/eng.traineddata.gz).
# VITE_TESSERACT_PATH=/tesseract

# Optional. The public address used in links you send (client document requests, intake links,
# invitations), e.g. https://app.renewaliq.com. Without it, links use whatever address the app is
# open on — on a Vercel preview that's the preview's long hostname.
# VITE_PUBLIC_APP_URL=
